# 10. Conclusion

The Investigation Module is the intelligence gathering layer of the Wizard system.

Its responsibility is not to modify code but to first understand the project completely. It converts an unknown repository into structured knowledge that other agents can use for planning and execution.

The complete pipeline is:

```
Repository
     |
     ↓
Scanner
     |
     ↓
Analyzer
     |
     ↓
Investigation Engine
     |
     ↓
Knowledge Representation
     |
     ↓
Planner Agent
     |
     ↓
Implementation
```

This architecture ensures that Wizard understands the existing system before suggesting or performing any changes.
